--- ffmpeg-xenon/README-XCLOUD360.md	1969-12-31 21:00:00.000000000 -0300
+++ ffmpeg-xenon-mt-altivec/README-XCLOUD360.md	2026-10-24 01:49:05.882306100 -0300
@@ -0,0 +1,183 @@
+# XCloud360: Xenon-safe AltiVec build of libavcodec 0.10.2 (frame threading)
+
+This tree is a copy of `~/ffmpeg-xenon-mt`, made on 2026-10-24. The original is untouched. It adds three things:
+
+- AltiVec (VMX) enabled for the H.264 decoder.
+- Every routine that would need an instruction the Xbox 360 Xenon does not implement is either rewritten with legal instructions or left in C.
+- The same hand-made pthread setup as `ffmpeg-xenon-mt`.
+
+All source changes are in `XCLOUD360-ALTIVEC.patch`, which is relative to `~/ffmpeg-xenon-mt`. To apply it to a fresh copy, run `cd <copy> && patch -p1 < XCLOUD360-ALTIVEC.patch`.
+
+## 1. Why a rewrite was needed
+
+The Xenon VMX128 unit does **not** implement these 22 AltiVec instructions:
+
+| Group | Instructions |
+|---|---|
+| Multiply-sum | `vmsumubm vmsummbm vmsumuhm vmsumuhs vmsumshm vmsumshs` |
+| Multiply-add | `vmhaddshs vmhraddshs vmladduhm` |
+| Multiply even/odd | `vmuleub vmuloub vmulesb vmulosb vmuleuh vmulouh vmulesh vmulosh` |
+| Sum-across | `vsum4ubs vsum4sbs vsum4shs vsum2sws vsumsws` |
+
+The evidence comes from three sources that agree:
+
+- The Free60 `gcc-9.2.0.diff` turns these patterns off with `TARGET_ALTIVEC && 0`.
+- Xenia leaves them `XEINSTRNOTIMPLEMENTED`.
+- G. Bobic listed them on gcc@gcc.gnu.org on 2007-08-21.
+
+In C terms, these intrinsics are unusable: `vec_msum`, `vec_msums`, `vec_mladd`, `vec_madds`, `vec_mradds`, `vec_mule`, `vec_mulo`, `vec_sum4s`, `vec_sum2s` and `vec_sums`.
+
+The earlier patch in `ffmpeg-xenon-mt` (`xen_altivec_asm.h` plus `XEN_ALTIVEC_MACRO_DISPATCH`) put those instructions back through inline asm. That build contained 531 of them and would trap on the console. **This tree removes it.**
+
+## 2. What changed (libavcodec/ppc only)
+
+| File | Change |
+|---|---|
+| `xcloud360_vmx.h` (new) | Defines `XCLOUD360_VMX_SAFE`. It is 1 automatically when `XENON` is defined. You can force it with `-DXCLOUD360_VMX_SAFE=1`, which the qemu reference build does. |
+| `types_altivec.h` | Removes the `xen_altivec_asm.h` include and the dispatch. Includes `<altivec.h>` and `xcloud360_vmx.h`. In safe mode it `#undef`s and **`#pragma GCC poison`s** all the intrinsics listed above, so any new use fails at compile time. This also holds for gcc 13, which would otherwise emit them. |
+| `xen_altivec_asm.h` | Deleted. |
+| `h264_template_altivec.c` | **qpel16 h/v lowpass:** `vec_mladd(x,20,16)` becomes `(x<<4)+(x<<2)+16`, and `vec_mladd(x,5,0)` becomes `(x<<2)+x`, both modulo 2^16 and bit-identical. **qpel16 hv lowpass, first stage:** the same change. **hv lowpass, second stage:** `vec_mule`/`vec_mulo` are replaced by `vec_unpackh`/`vec_unpackl` to s32, ×20 and ×5 by shift and add, then `vec_packs` and `vec_packsu` in natural lane order (the `mperm` shuffle is no longer needed). **chroma mc8 (put/avg):** a new Xenon-safe version computes in single-precision float (`vcfux`/`vmaddfp`/`vctuxs`). This is exact because every partial sum is an integer of at most 64·255+32 < 2^24. The original code and the macros that use `vec_mladd` are kept under `#if !XCLOUD360_VMX_SAFE`. The VC-1 chroma variant fails with `#error` in safe mode (VC-1 is not built here). |
+| `h264_altivec.c` | Adds the `XC_MUL20/XC_MUL5` macros (16- and 32-bit) and `xc_mul_s16_f()`, an exact float multiply for \|a·w\| < 2^15. **weight/biweight 16 and 8** use `xc_mul_s16_f` instead of `vec_mladd`, so they stay vectorised. Init is unchanged: idct, luma deblock, qpel, chroma, weight and biweight are all installed. |
+| `dsputil_altivec.c` | sad16/sad8/sse/pix_norm1/pix_sum and hadamard8_diff (which use vsum*, vmsum* and vmladduhm) are compiled out in safe mode and their init entries are skipped. All of them are encoder-only metrics. |
+| `dsputil_ppc.c` | In safe mode, skips `ff_int_init_altivec`, `gmc1` and the MPEG `ff_idct_put/add_altivec` block. H.264 never uses any of them. |
+| `idct_altivec.c`, `int_altivec.c`, `gmc_altivec.c` | Body compiled out in safe mode. |
+| `mpegvideo_altivec.c` | `dct_unquantize_h263_altivec` and its install are compiled out in safe mode. |
+
+The configure step, which is not part of the patch, is in `xcloud360/cfg-xenon-altivec.sh`:
+
+- It uses the original `ffmpeg-xenon-mt` configure line, minus `--disable-altivec` and plus `-maltivec -mabi=altivec -mno-vrsave`.
+- It then re-applies the hand pthread edits: `config.h` HAVE_PTHREADS/HAVE_THREADS 1, `config.mak` HAVE_PTHREADS/HAVE_THREADS=yes, and the `pthread.o: -D_POSIX_THREADS=1` line in `libavcodec/Makefile`, which was already present.
+- configure itself adds `-fno-tree-vectorize`, so the auto-vectoriser cannot generate `vmuleuh`/`vmulesh` from plain C.
+- `-mno-vrsave` keeps `mfspr/mtspr 256` (VRSAVE) out of the code.
+- `config.h` differs from `ffmpeg-xenon-mt` only in `HAVE_ALTIVEC 1` and `HAVE_ALTIVEC_H 1`.
+
+### H.264 paths: what runs AltiVec now (Xenon build)
+
+| AltiVec (legal instructions only) | Still C |
+|---|---|
+| qpel16 MC, all 16 positions, put and avg (16x16 partitions) | qpel8 and qpel4 (sub-16x16 partitions): there is no AltiVec version in 0.10.2 |
+| chroma mc8 put/avg (float, exact) | chroma mc4/mc2 |
+| h264_idct_add, idct_add16, add16intra, add8, idct_dc_add (and idct8, which High profile uses) | intra prediction (h264pred) |
+| luma deblock v/h | chroma deblock (no AltiVec in 0.10.2) |
+| weight/biweight 16/8 (float, exact) | CAVLC/CABAC entropy decode |
+| put/avg pixels16, avg pixels8, pixels8/16 xy2, clear_block, add_bytes | |
+
+## 3. Build and use
+
+```
+cd ~/ffmpeg-xenon-mt-altivec
+export PATH=$HOME/devkitxenon/bin:$HOME/devkitxenon/usr/bin:$PATH
+make -j2 libavutil/libavutil.a libavcodec/libavcodec.a   # libavformat is not needed (and does not build for xenon: usleep)
+```
+
+To link the app, override the decoder dir. It is used with `-I$(FFMPEG_DIR) -L.../libavcodec -L.../libavutil -lavcodec -lavutil`:
+
+```
+cd app/h264play && make FFMPEG_DIR=$HOME/ffmpeg-xenon-mt-altivec
+```
+
+This was checked on a copy of app/h264play 0.14.4-split in `~/scratch/wf/trackA/applink`. It links cleanly, and the ELF has 0 unsupported instructions.
+
+## 4. Opcode audit (proof that no Xenon-unsupported instruction is present)
+
+```
+BAD="vmsumubm|vmsummbm|vmsumuhm|vmsumuhs|vmsumshm|vmsumshs|vmhaddshs|vmhraddshs|vmladduhm|vmuleub|vmuloub|vmulesb|vmulosb|vmuleuh|vmulouh|vmulesh|vmulosh|vsum4ubs|vsum4sbs|vsum4shs|vsum2sws|vsumsws"
+~/devkitxenon/bin/xenon-objdump -d -M altivec libavcodec/libavcodec.a | grep -cwE "$BAD"
